WEBVTT

00:02:59.046 --> 00:03:00.788
As of the end of last year,

00:03:00.788 --> 00:03:03.155
1,314 men

00:03:03.155 --> 00:03:05.370
had run under four minutes in the mile,

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.820
but like Jesse Owens,

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.562
Sir Roger Bannister ran on soft cinders

00:03:09.562 --> 00:03:11.386
that stole far more energy from his legs

00:03:11.386 --> 00:03:13.749
than the synthetic tracks of today.

00:03:13.749 --> 00:03:15.249
So I consulted biomechanics experts

00:03:15.249 --> 00:03:17.813
to find out how much slower it is to run on cinders

00:03:17.813 --> 00:03:19.071
than synthetic tracks,

00:03:19.071 --> 00:03:22.471
and their consensus that it's
one and a half percent slower.

00:03:22.471 --> 00:03:25.758
So if you apply a one and a half
percent slowdown conversion

00:03:25.758 --> 00:03:27.944
to every man who ran his sub-four mile

00:03:27.944 --> 00:03:29.388
on a synthetic track,

00:03:29.388 --> 00:03:31.084
this is what happens.